<title>USA: Cumberland Cty, N.C., sets $98 mln bond referendum.</title>
<headline>Cumberland Cty, N.C., sets $98 mln bond referendum.</headline>
<dateline>FAYETTEVILLE, N.C. 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's Cumberland County tentatively set a $98 million school bond referendum for Oct 7.</p>
<p>The county commission approved the date Monday, anticipating that Oct 7 would be the primary election date for other municipal races.</p>
<p>The date could change if there are not enough candidates to require a primary.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
